WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.867 --> 00:00:12.135
intensifying the CIA director

00:00:12.269 --> 00:00:13.036
says the next few months will be

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.540
crucial for the outcome.

00:00:16.673 --> 00:00:18.375
&gt;&gt; I think the next six months

00:00:18.509 --> 00:00:20.410
it seems to me, and it's our

00:00:20.544 --> 00:00:22.479
assessment at CIA, are going to

00:00:22.613 --> 00:00:22.880
be critical.

00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:24.147
Putin I think is betting right

00:00:24.281 --> 00:00:25.716
now that he can make time work

00:00:25.849 --> 00:00:26.683
for him.

00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:29.653
He is betting that he can grind

00:00:29.653 --> 00:00:31.188
down Ukrainians, that political

00:00:31.321 --> 00:00:32.923
fatigue is going to set in.

00:00:33.056 --> 00:00:34.925
We do not assess that Putin is

00:00:35.058 --> 00:00:37.027
serious about negotiations.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.663
The key is on the battlefield in

00:00:39.663 --> 00:00:43.233
the next six months it seems to

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:44.334
us.

00:00:44.468 --> 00:00:46.503
Puncturing Putin's hubris.

00:00:46.637 --> 00:00:48.005
Making clear he is not going to

00:00:48.138 --> 00:00:50.374
be able to advance further in

00:00:50.507 --> 00:00:52.009
Ukraine, but as every month goes

00:00:52.142 --> 00:00:53.677
by he runs a greater and greater

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:56.346
risk of losing the territory

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:57.047
that he has illegally seized

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.316
from Ukraine so far.

00:00:59.683 --> 00:01:00.884
&gt;&gt; I want to bring in the former

00:01:01.018 --> 00:01:02.486
European affairs director at the

00:01:02.619 --> 00:01:04.521
national security council

00:01:04.655 --> 00:01:06.290
retired lieutenant colonel Alex

00:01:06.423 --> 00:01:08.258
vin man, the author of here

00:01:08.392 --> 00:01:09.693
right matters an American story.

00:01:09.693 --> 00:01:10.794
Thank you so much for joining me

00:01:10.928 --> 00:01:11.228
this morning.

00:01:11.361 --> 00:01:12.062
Good to talk to you.

00:01:12.195 --> 00:01:13.830
I wonder what you made of the

00:01:13.964 --> 00:01:17.134
assessment from the CIA

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:17.701
director.

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:21.705
&gt;&gt; I think that the ambassadors

00:01:21.838 --> 00:01:23.707
and director's assessment is

00:01:23.707 --> 00:01:24.474
very, very good.

00:01:24.608 --> 00:01:26.310
My question is, what are we

00:01:26.443 --> 00:01:28.378
doing to make this very critical

00:01:28.512 --> 00:01:30.847
next six months increasingly

00:01:30.981 --> 00:01:31.815
difficult for Vladimir Putin.

00:01:31.949 --> 00:01:34.651
The fact is that this next six

00:01:34.785 --> 00:01:37.020
months the Russians are going to

00:01:37.154 --> 00:01:38.589
potentially start another

00:01:38.722 --> 00:01:39.723
offensive, take more territory.

00:01:39.856 --> 00:01:41.925
The Ukrainians are going to have

00:01:42.059 --> 00:01:43.727
to blunt that attack and move on

00:01:43.794 --> 00:01:47.731
the offensive and start to take

00:01:47.864 --> 00:01:48.098
territory.

00:01:48.231 --> 00:01:49.299
These slow flows of tanks, the

00:01:49.733 --> 00:01:51.401
fact that we are providing

00:01:51.735 --> 00:01:53.003
Abrams and they won't get there

00:01:53.136 --> 00:01:54.905
for six months is not

00:01:55.038 --> 00:01:55.305
sufficient.

00:01:55.739 --> 00:01:56.006
Signaling those tanks coming

00:01:56.139 --> 00:02:00.277
just to release the German

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:00.877
leopard tanks and other

00:02:01.011 --> 00:02:02.212
countries providing tanks is

00:02:02.346 --> 00:02:04.348
not -- that's a what happened in

00:02:04.481 --> 00:02:04.648
2008.

00:02:04.781 --> 00:02:08.051
We signaled we wanted Ukraine to

00:02:08.185 --> 00:02:11.054
join nato and all that did was

00:02:11.188 --> 00:02:13.223
precipitate Russia's increased

00:02:13.357 --> 00:02:13.757
aggression.

00:02:13.757 --> 00:02:15.859
We have to take firm action

00:02:15.993 --> 00:02:19.763
which is provide Ukraine the

00:02:19.796 --> 00:02:20.297
equipment it needs, that

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:23.166
includes planes, drones, that

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:23.900
includes accelerating the pace

00:02:24.034 --> 00:02:24.668
of the delivery of these tanks,

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:26.637
and that can be done.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:28.138
It's just a matter of will.

00:02:28.271 --> 00:02:29.773
&gt;&gt; And you said you believe the

00:02:29.873 --> 00:02:31.775
flow of this equipment and these

00:02:31.908 --> 00:02:33.343
weapons to Ukraine is kind of

00:02:33.777 --> 00:02:35.779
resulting in this incremental

00:02:35.779 --> 00:02:36.046
escalation.

00:02:36.179 --> 00:02:36.947
You write in foreign affairs

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.182
that western reluctance to fully

00:02:39.316 --> 00:02:40.651
support Ukraine and defeat

00:02:40.784 --> 00:02:42.185
Russia undercuts Ukraine's

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:43.787
ability to conduct an offends

00:02:43.887 --> 00:02:46.256
and cause the war to stretch

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:46.957
deep into 2023.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.725
It seems like you are saying if

00:02:48.859 --> 00:02:50.694
it they provided more sooner,

00:02:50.827 --> 00:02:53.363
this could end sooner?

00:02:53.797 --> 00:02:54.531
&gt;&gt; That's very true.

00:02:54.665 --> 00:02:56.266
But I am also concerned about

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:56.667
the future.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.269
It's not just the fact that we

00:02:59.403 --> 00:03:01.805
allowed this war to stretch out

00:03:01.838 --> 00:03:03.807
many, many months more than it

00:03:03.807 --> 00:03:04.141
needs to be.

00:03:04.274 --> 00:03:05.876
It's that the next six, nine

00:03:06.009 --> 00:03:07.411
months are going to be

00:03:07.811 --> 00:03:08.445
particularly dangerous.

00:03:08.578 --> 00:03:10.447
We are probably going to face an

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:11.815
increasingly erratic Vladimir

00:03:11.882 --> 00:03:14.051
Putin where he believes that his

00:03:14.184 --> 00:03:16.486
crown jewel, the crimea

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:17.888
peninsula, is going to be under

00:03:18.021 --> 00:03:19.823
threat and what actions he takes

00:03:19.923 --> 00:03:20.090
then.

00:03:20.223 --> 00:03:21.058
I feel very confident in saying

00:03:21.191 --> 00:03:23.126
he is not going to escalate to

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.829
any nuclear options because that

00:03:25.829 --> 00:03:27.264
would be the end of his regime.

00:03:27.397 --> 00:03:28.365
That's the point he starts to

00:03:28.498 --> 00:03:30.734
really seriously consider that

00:03:30.867 --> 00:03:31.068
option.

00:03:31.201 --> 00:03:32.269
Not just threaten it.

00:03:32.402 --> 00:03:34.137
Not just to use that as a means

00:03:34.271 --> 00:03:35.939
to get the west to back down,

00:03:36.073 --> 00:03:37.040
but starts to consider the

00:03:37.174 --> 00:03:37.974
option seriously.

00:03:38.108 --> 00:03:39.443
If that's the biggest thing we

00:03:39.843 --> 00:03:41.878
want to avoid, this potential

00:03:42.012 --> 00:03:43.513
existential crisis, we need to

00:03:43.847 --> 00:03:46.583
make sure we don't go this road

00:03:46.717 --> 00:03:47.517
of incremental escalation and

00:03:47.851 --> 00:03:49.019
give the Ukrainians what they

00:03:49.152 --> 00:03:50.954
need, the means to threaten the

00:03:51.088 --> 00:03:53.857
peninsula and then force Putin

00:03:53.957 --> 00:03:56.326
to negotiate in earnest, like

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:57.427
the director of central

00:03:57.861 --> 00:03:59.396
intelligence said, he is not

00:03:59.529 --> 00:03:59.863
serious yet.

00:03:59.963 --> 00:04:02.099
He will absolutely get serious

00:04:02.232 --> 00:04:04.000
when crimea is under threat and

00:04:04.134 --> 00:04:05.969
the Ukrainians liberate more

00:04:06.103 --> 00:04:06.336
territory.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:07.871
The sooner we get there, the

00:04:07.938 --> 00:04:09.372
less chance of escalation and

00:04:09.506 --> 00:04:11.875
less risk to spill over into a

00:04:11.875 --> 00:04:12.342
confrontation with nato.

00:04:12.476 --> 00:04:15.879
&gt;&gt; You think the U.S. Should

00:04:15.879 --> 00:04:17.047
send the fighter jets?

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.749
&gt;&gt; We should be training the

00:04:18.882 --> 00:04:20.050
Ukrainians on fighter jets.

00:04:20.183 --> 00:04:21.418
If we keep saying that it takes

00:04:21.551 --> 00:04:23.420
months and months to prepare the

00:04:23.553 --> 00:04:24.788
Ukrainians for these advanced

00:04:24.921 --> 00:04:26.256
capabilities, which it does, we

00:04:26.389 --> 00:04:28.091
should be training them now on

00:04:28.225 --> 00:04:30.193
the prospect they may need them

00:04:30.327 --> 00:04:33.063
six months from now.

00:04:33.196 --> 00:04:33.897
We should have been doing the

00:04:33.897 --> 00:04:34.865
tank training a long time ago.

00:04:34.998 --> 00:04:36.666
What disturbs me, symptoms come

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.368
in without logistical support.

00:04:38.502 --> 00:04:39.236
All the support that the

00:04:39.369 --> 00:04:40.804
Ukrainians get, they get it

00:04:40.937 --> 00:04:42.105
outside of Poland.

00:04:42.239 --> 00:04:44.674
Everything else is done through

00:04:44.808 --> 00:04:45.976
what we call telemedicine, you

00:04:46.109 --> 00:04:48.211
call up and show the Ukrainians

00:04:48.345 --> 00:04:49.045
what's broken on a screen and

00:04:49.179 --> 00:04:52.382
they have to say, okay, well, we

00:04:52.516 --> 00:04:54.384
need these parts and it takes a

00:04:54.518 --> 00:04:56.186
look time to get systems fixed.

00:04:56.319 --> 00:04:58.522
Supporting a war from 800

00:04:58.655 --> 00:04:59.923
kilometers away is

00:04:59.956 --> 00:05:00.257
unsustainable.

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:02.292
We need to provide logistics.

